<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="b95e5f83">&lt;p&gt;
    This project classifications document defines criteria for three different sized projects. Effective project managers
    use the appropriate number of processes to meet the rigor and discipline needed for the size of the project. Use this
    when writing a project plan, to help determine core and discretionary documentation based on the size and scope of a
    project. If clarification is needed, please consult the executive in charge.&lt;br /&gt;
    &lt;br /&gt;
    There are three project classifications: large, medium and small. Note: Large projects may also be referred to as
    “enterprise” projects. The below classifications provide guidance on project classification, but the optional items
    imply the need for more rigorous discipline and would demand the use of more tools to manage the risk.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table title=&quot;&quot; cellspacing=&quot;0&quot; cellpadding=&quot;2&quot; width=&quot;85%&quot; border=&quot;1&quot;&gt;
    &lt;tbody&gt;
        &lt;tr&gt;
            &lt;th scope=&quot;col&quot; abbr=&quot;&quot;&gt;
                If the project meets these criteria
            &lt;/th&gt;
            &lt;th scope=&quot;col&quot; abbr=&quot;&quot;&gt;
                Then the project is classified as
            &lt;/th&gt;
        &lt;/tr&gt;
        &lt;tr&gt;
            &lt;td&gt;
                &lt;p&gt;
                    At least two of the following are true:
                &lt;/p&gt;
                &lt;ul&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Cumulative effort hours: &amp;gt; 80,000
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Vendor part of project team
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Global impact (project creates a global product or service or project has global reach)
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Duration &amp;gt; one year
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Project creates new product or service
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        New technology is being used on project
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Global Delivery Services integration
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        High complexity*
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                &lt;/ul&gt;
            &lt;/td&gt;
            &lt;td&gt;
                Large
            &lt;/td&gt;
        &lt;/tr&gt;
        &lt;tr&gt;
            &lt;td&gt;
                &lt;p&gt;
                    At least two of the following are true:
                &lt;/p&gt;
                &lt;ul&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Cumulative effort hours: 40,000 – 80,000
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Vendor part of project team
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Impacts multiple geographies
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Duration six months – one year
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Project creates new product or service
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        New technology is being used on project
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Moderate complexity*&lt;br /&gt;
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                &lt;/ul&gt;
            &lt;/td&gt;
            &lt;td&gt;
                Medium
            &lt;/td&gt;
        &lt;/tr&gt;
        &lt;tr&gt;
            &lt;td&gt;
                &lt;p&gt;
                    At least one of the following is true:
                &lt;/p&gt;
                &lt;ul&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Cumulative effort hours: 1,200 – 4,000
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Duration &amp;lt; six months
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                &lt;/ul&gt;
            &lt;/td&gt;
            &lt;td&gt;
                Small
            &lt;/td&gt;
        &lt;/tr&gt;
    &lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    * Complexity includes evaluating the following factors for each particular project: risk and impact to EY, multiple
    stakeholders and results the project needs to create.&lt;br /&gt;
    &lt;br /&gt;
    Project documentation&lt;br /&gt;
    The below documentation requirements have been defined for the three classifications. However, the information provided
    is a recommended list to start with. Practitioners are encouraged to apply judgment as to documents needed, and the
    level of detail required to complete same, based on the unique nature of the projects. The level of review for
    documents serving as deliverables should also be determined for quality planning purposes. In general, the respective
    core documents are produced on each project. The discretionary documents are additional and based on the judgment of
    the project manager.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;
    Large
&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;table title=&quot;&quot; cellspacing=&quot;0&quot; cellpadding=&quot;2&quot; width=&quot;85%&quot; border=&quot;1&quot;&gt;
    &lt;tbody&gt;
        &lt;tr&gt;
            &lt;th scope=&quot;col&quot; abbr=&quot;&quot;&gt;
                Core documents
            &lt;/th&gt;
            &lt;th scope=&quot;col&quot; abbr=&quot;&quot;&gt;
                Discretionary documents
            &lt;/th&gt;
        &lt;/tr&gt;
        &lt;tr&gt;
            &lt;td&gt;
                &lt;ul&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Project charter (detailed): PM04 Project
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Charter Template - Detailed
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Project plan/project schedule: PM20
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Project Plan and Progress Tracker
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Project stakeholder register: PM09
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Stakeholder Register Template
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Project communications calendar/plan: PM13 Communications Calendar Template
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Project roles &amp; responsibilities/RACI (see note): PM07 Project Management Role Guide and PM08
                        Project Management RACI Chart
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Project budget: PM10 Project Estimation Worksheet and PM11 Project Budget Request Form
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Project resource plan: PM12 Project Resource Request Form&lt;br /&gt;
                        RAID (risks, assumptions, issues and dependencies): PM14 RAID Log&lt;br /&gt;
                        Project status report: PM22 Status
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Report Template&lt;br /&gt;
                        Project change request &amp; project change log: PM15 Project Scope Change Log and PM16 Project
                        Scope Change Template
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Project lessons learned: PM25 Lessons Learned Template
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Project closure: PM24 Project Closure Template
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                &lt;/ul&gt;
            &lt;/td&gt;
            &lt;td&gt;
                &lt;ul&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Project scorecard: This document is not a core deliverable as the use of it varies by project. It
                        is utilized for reporting status for a program with multiple projects, or a project with multiple
                        work streams.
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Lessons learned log: This document is not a deliverable as the use of it varies by project. It is a
                        repository of the lessons learned during a project.
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Project contact list: This document is not a deliverable as the use of it varies by project. It
                        contains contact information for project team members. Basic information captured includes the name
                        and phone number of team members.
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Meeting decisions &amp; actions: EM32 Key Decision Log Template.
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Project milestone schedule: PM18 Project Milestone Template
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Project financials: PM19 Project Financial Tracking Template
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Work product: PM21 Work Product Tracking Template
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Project quality review: PM23 Project Quality Review Form
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                &lt;/ul&gt;
            &lt;/td&gt;
        &lt;/tr&gt;
    &lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;
    Medium&lt;br /&gt;
    &lt;br /&gt;
&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;table title=&quot;&quot; cellspacing=&quot;0&quot; cellpadding=&quot;2&quot; width=&quot;85%&quot; border=&quot;1&quot;&gt;
    &lt;tbody&gt;
        &lt;tr&gt;
            &lt;th scope=&quot;col&quot; abbr=&quot;&quot;&gt;
                Core documents
            &lt;/th&gt;
            &lt;th scope=&quot;col&quot; abbr=&quot;&quot;&gt;
                Discretionary documents
            &lt;/th&gt;
        &lt;/tr&gt;
        &lt;tr&gt;
            &lt;td&gt;
                &lt;ul&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Project charter (detailed): PM04 Project Charter Template - Detailed
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Project plan/project schedule: PM20 Project Plan and Progress Tracker
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Project stakeholder register: PM09 Stakeholder Register Template
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        RAID (risks, assumptions, issues and dependencies): PM14 RAID Log
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Project status report: PM22 Status Report Template
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Project change request &amp; project change log:
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        PM15 Project Scope Change Log and PM16 Project Scope Change Template
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Project lessons learned: PM25 Lessons Learned Template
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Project closure: PM24 Project Closure Template&lt;br /&gt;
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                &lt;/ul&gt;
            &lt;/td&gt;
            &lt;td&gt;
                &lt;ul&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Project management RACI: PM08 Project Management RACI Chart
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Project communications calendar/plan: PM13 Communications Calendar Template
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Project scorecard: This document is not a core deliverable as the use of it varies by project. It
                        is utilized for reporting status for a program with multiple projects, or a project with multiple
                        work streams.
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Lessons learned log: This document is not a deliverable as the use of it varies by project. It is a
                        repository of the lessons learned during a project.
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Project contact list: This document is not a deliverable as the use of it varies by project. It
                        contains contact information for project team members. Basic information captured includes the name
                        and phone number of team members.
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Meeting decisions &amp; actions: EM32 Key Decision Log Template
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Project milestone schedule: PM18 Project Milestone Template
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Project financials: PM19 Project Financial Tracking Template
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Work product: PM21 Work Product Tracking Template
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Project quality review: PM23 Project Quality Review Form
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                &lt;/ul&gt;
            &lt;/td&gt;
        &lt;/tr&gt;
    &lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;
